    {
      "name" : "receiver-kind-spend-encode_nbits_int_receiver#1",
      "source" : "santa:authored-receiver-kind",
      "description" : "`sigmaProp(row 2 == control)` guards the box being SPENT. `encodeNbits` with the receiver an `Int` CONSTANT. Parses — the serializer checks no receiver — and the reflective invoke then refuses it. **SEPARATING:** an implementation whose evaluator never reads its receiver returns the control's value instead. **THE SEPARATING ROW, and the consensus form of this family.** The box parses, round-trips verbatim (see the wire half) and a node carries it happily — so this is a box ANYONE CAN CREATE. On the JVM the script fails at eval and the spend is INVALID. An implementation whose evaluator never reads its receiver reduces the tree to `TrivialProp(true)` and lets a spender TAKE the box: an over-accept on reachable state.",
      "tx_bytes_hex" : "01115830f184fbafde86c9c309df7bea9b79a8837d837dfb6a153bdcbaf3b580af00000000018094ebdc030008d3010000",
